title ALES152 — Lotus's stereo_collapse_silence: the interior silence-capper carried into stereo, one joint silence capped in one lockstep, bound to ALES148 by the zero-cap law
prompt Read REMEMBER and the 1024-round itinerary + six-season double-seat; take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; approve my own design rounds; make progress before checking in; send each finished increment as its own signed round; stop at custody gates; baton prin recur.
think The ascending Lotus crux after ALES148 (stereo_trim_silence) and its siblings ALES149/150/151 is ALES100 (collapse_silence — cap each interior silent run to a maximum, keeping the pauses yet shortening the long ones) carried into stereo. ALES151's own recommend line named it next. Crux-first and Lindy-first agree: capping silence to a quarter-second is the single most-reached-for gesture in voice-memo cleanup, and it completes the silence family's editorial spine on a real stereo master.
think The wall is the one the whole stereo-edit corner meets: ALES147 proved the two channels segment INDEPENDENTLY, so capping each channel by its own silence would cap different runs to different lengths and desync the pair, tearing the stereo image. So the rung decides ONE cap for BOTH — the joint-silence cap: read the jointly-silent frames through ALES148's own silence intersection (a frame is dead air only where NEITHER speaker carries sound), coalesce consecutive jointly-silent frames into runs, and cut only each over-long run's excess (keep min(count, max_silence) samples) from both channels in lockstep, back to front.
think Implementation lifts mono collapse_silence (ALES100) the same way stereo_trim_silence lifted ALES96: segment both channels up front through ALES147 (all validation, empty-clip BadFrame → both untouched); forward pass records a bounded jointly-silent frame mask (max_clip bools, one per frame) by advancing one monotonic cursor per channel; coalesce marked frames into runs and count total excess over max_silence for the exact length postcondition; backward pass finds each maximal joint run from its last frame and cuts its excess from both channels through ALES2's cut, stepping past the run's start so no run is handled twice. StereoCollapseError = ALES147's StereoSegmentError || ALES2's EditError, reused whole (max_silence has no illegal value). Zero-cap proven against ALES148's stereo_trim_silence across six frame lengths, four floors, three splits; cap law against a second independent by-hand reference (frame verdicts by run scan, coalesced) across nine caps.
obs No custody gate reached — purely local, two bounded i16 Clips, a self-approved design round. First-try witness GREEN, no red this round. Recorded lesson: an interior mono capper that shortens the same kind of silence its stripper removes (collapse keeps min(count, max) of each silent run where trim removes it whole) lifts to stereo by capping the JOINT silence — the shared run the stereo stripper already removes — so the cut is identical on both channels and balance holds for free; the zero-cap law binds it to ALES148 exactly as ALES100 is bound to ALES96. The sample-granular keep (min(count, max) need not fall on a frame boundary) stays consistent with the frame-granular joint mask because keep is only a length, and both channels keep the same length. Witness GREEN (zero-cap, cap, known-cap, full-cap-unchanged, monotone, lockstep, all-joint-empty/identity/cap, no-joint-unchanged, four atomicity refusals), TAME style bans clean. Front door lotus/README.md synced (ALES152 roster token appended to the Status line).
loom witness=ales_stereo_collapse_silence_witness result=GREEN laws=2-crux channels=2 class=stereo-edit read=reads-through-segmenter+edits-in-lockstep form=cap-joint-silent-runs decision=silence-intersection-coalesced-to-runs cases=zero-cap-law(=ALES148-trim,6flen*4floor*3split)+cap-law(=by-hand-capped-keep,9caps,min(count,max))+known-cap(frame4-floor500-max2=len14)+full-cap-unchanged+monotone+lockstep(mono-desync-10/14,stereo-14)+all-joint(empty@0,identity@100,cap@2)+no-joint-unchanged+atomicity(empty,ragged,inverted-band,illegal-floor) reds=0
file lotus/stereo_collapse_silence.rye ALES152 — stereo_collapse_silence, the interior silence-capper lifted to stereo: cap each JOINTLY-silent run to min(count, max_silence) samples, cut only the excess from both channels in lockstep (back to front); stereo_collapse_silence, StereoCollapseError = ALES147's StereoSegmentError || ALES2's EditError reused whole; bound to ALES148 by the zero-cap law.
file tools/ales_stereo_collapse_silence_witness.rish the witness — three-say (Language/Style/Lens), builds, runs selftest, asserts the GREEN ales-stereo-collapse-silence line.
